      "name": "Is a new Sovereign Gold Bond issue coming in 2026?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No. The last tranche was SGB 2023-24 Series IV in February 2024, and no new tranche has been announced since. Existing bonds can be held to maturity (8 years), redeemed early with RBI after 5 years on interest dates, or sold on NSE/BSE."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How can I buy SGB now?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Only on the secondary market. Listed SGB series trade on NSE and BSE and can be bought through a demat account, usually at a small discount or premium to the market price of gold."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is it mandatory to redeem SGB after 8 years?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Though the tenor of the bond is 8 years, early encashment/redemption of the bond is allowed after fifth year from the date of issue on coupon payment dates. The bond will be tradable on Exchanges, if held in demat form."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I exit SGB before 5 years?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Although the Sovereign Gold Bond (SGB) has a tenor of 8 years, it can be redeemed prematurely on coupon payment dates after the 5th year from the date of issue. A charge of ₹150 + 18% GST will be imposed for rematerialisation or redemption."
      }
    }
  ]
